  "vm07": {
    "set": "V-must",
    "hits": [
      "The in-memory adapter decides whether a guest may book (one booking per guest per day) and refuses by raising ValueError. That policy belongs in the command's handle(), and a guest-caused refusal should be a returned failure, not an exception. Nothing in CreateBooking catches the ValueError, so a second booking by the same guest on a day would crash the request.",
      "The SQLite adapter's save() does a read (`_select`) and then a write (insert). It also enforces the booking policy and raises ValueError for something a guest can cause. The command should read the guest's bookings that day, return a failure such as a new member of CreateBookingFailure, and only then call save()."
    ],
